+      "pin_review_2026_08_29_seat46": "PIN HELD at 7529fdaaf, and NOT repointed to the v7 lineage in this seat. 3 offers exactly three verdicts and a re-pin is allowed only for SKIP; this is neither. The 2026-08-28 fork-currency review establishes that `prism` was REPOINTED onto the v7 lineage and that our pin is NO LONGER AN ANCESTOR of the ref head (`compare/7529fdaaf...prism` = diverged, merge_base 8a963fc10 of 2026-06-07), so currency's prisml row is measuring ACROSS A FORK POINT - the 1108 is divergent-history arithmetic, not a distance, and the real fork-authored surface against upstream is 44. A 3 increment re-pin is therefore not available AT ALL here, regardless of TAKE status: advancing to e311ed38f would silently discard the v5-side review record written by lanes 143/152/156/158/161. This is base-move-shaped, not increment-shaped. PRESIDENT/HQ ITEM, unchanged and NOT ruled by this seat: pick the lineage (prism-v5 = the historical record, prism-v7/prism = the live line), and if v7, re-scope a fresh surface against upstream or the merge-base. The standing blocker 9ca265a57 is NOT in the new prism (it survives only on retired prism-v5); a7cc29645 may supersede it - TO BE CHECKED, not ruled.",
       "pin_review_2026_08_20_lane161": "PIN STILL HELD at 7529fdaaf, both standing rows re-checked at this fetch (prisml/prism tip unchanged at 9ca265a57). (1) 4dd165625 draft-context bias fix: functionally CLOSED - lane-158 re-derived it at our centralized speculative-params seam (its commit 8a05ba3c8, now in the series via the kcache patches) - but the pin measures review of THEIR tip, and 9ca265a57 still blocks it. (2) 9ca265a57 __byte_perm Q2_0 extraction: the hold is now SHARPER than lane-156's structural-port blocker. Our own AGENTS.md pitfalls list documents that __byte_perm WITH CONSTANT SELECTORS folds differently on some toolchains and silently produced NMSE ~1.0 garbage in mmvq-tq.cu, with an explicit do-not-clean-up warning on the shift code. Porting a __byte_perm OPTIMIZATION into that hazard class, re-derived by hand against our post-refactor mmq-load-tiles.cuh, UNBUILT (no CUDA device on this rig) and UNSWEEPABLE, is the exact silent-garbage recipe the pitfall records. RECOMMENDATION, not a rung: port it on a CUDA-capable seat with a test-backend-ops execution proof, or decline it as an optimization whose risk profile exceeds its unmeasured gain. UNKNOWN-with-blocker means the pin stays.",
       "pin_review_2026_08_19_lane158": "PIN DELIBERATELY HELD at 7529fdaaf while lane-158 TAKES the K-cache mean-centering capability from PrismML's separate v6 lineage and the default-branch follow-up 4dd165625. SOURCE-CENSUS CORRECTION: the lane brief's `1076 new lines in 8 files` is exact only for the EIGHT wholly new files; the full feature range dea384100^..b075a360c is 1377 insertions / 2 deletions across 19 files, with ELEVEN existing touchpoints (the brief and lane-156 review said eight). Every one of the eight new files was read in full and the complete feature-range diff over the eleven existing files was reviewed before porting. TAKEN onto kcache158/2026-08-19 in four source commits: 6b9a2e121 (compile flag GGML_ARIFI_KV_MEANCENTER, default OFF, port), 932d33fe1 (ArifiLabs hardening: domain-separated SHA-256 over every byte of every ordered GGUF split; calibration schema/model/k_rot/geometry checks; missing, partial, extra, wrong-model and wrong-basis artifacts refuse load), 8a05ba3c8 (4dd165625 re-derived at this fork's centralized speculative-params seam so an external draft context never inherits the target calibration), and f56cf26f1 (Vulkan pre/post tensor probe plus bench-pure, three-replication A/B runner/verifier). The upstream 4dd fix was NOT silently treated as part of v6: it is not an ancestor of b075a360c and was audited/applied separately. PIN WHY HELD: tools/arifi-sync tracks the real default ref prisml/prism, whose tip also contains 9ca265a57; that CUDA __byte_perm candidate remains the structural, post-refactor mmq-load-tiles.cuh manual-port blocker documented by lane-156. Advancing to the ref tip would falsely close that blocked TAKE, while changing the ref would violate the registered-default-branch contract and hide default-branch drift. SOURCE/HARNESS EFFECT CHECKED: patch-series generation/check/replay and arifi_sync_check are GREEN; Python A/B verifier selftest accepts a good fixture and returns RED on a planted overlap. NATIVE BUILD, OFF byte identity, exact-model calibration, Vulkan tensor execution, PPL, decode speed, full backend sweep, and independent checker remain UNMEASURED in this managed seat and are explicitly HQ-OWNED; no accuracy, speed, or context-raise claim is made here.",
       "pin_review_2026_08_18_lane156": "PIN DELIBERATELY HELD at 7529fdaaf for the SECOND wave, and the reason is now SHARPER than lane-152's, not merely repeated. Both commits in 7529fdaaf..9ca265a57 were re-reviewed against arifi/main at b10488. (1) 4dd165625 'server: do not propagate kv-mean-center bias to draft model contexts' - SKIP-UNTIL-FEATURE, re-CHECKED at this tip: `kv_mean_center` appears in our tree in exactly THREE places and every one of them is pin-review prose (tools/arifi-sync/sources.json and two banked patch files). Zero code. The fix patches a prisml capability we have never ingested; it rides in with the feature and never before it. (2) 9ca265a57 'cuda: extract Q2_0 elements via __byte_perm' - A REAL TAKE CANDIDATE ON OUR OWN TYPE, BLOCKED, and the blocker is now NAMED with the file: `git apply --3way` reaches 'Applied with conflicts' on BOTH files. vecdotq.cuh conflicts are COMMENT-ONLY (3 hunks, all comment text) - that half is portable. mmq.cuh is the blocker and it is STRUCTURAL, not textual: prisml's own commit message says 'Upstream's tile-load lives in mmq-load-tiles.cuh after their MMQ refactor; ours is still in mmq.cuh, so this is a manual port'. WE ARE ON THE POST-REFACTOR SIDE - our load_tiles_q2_0 is in ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq-load-tiles.cuh (which prisml does not have as a file at all) and our mmq-load-tiles.cuh:114-117 carries the QK2_0 blocks_per_iter/scale_entries arithmetic. So their manual port must be RE-DERIVED against mmq-load-tiles.cuh; it cannot be applied. THE PIN IS HELD RATHER THAN ADVANCED because the runbook only allows a re-pin for SKIP, and this is a blocked TAKE, not a SKIP. The unblocking work is bounded: re-derive the __byte_perm decode against our mmq-load-tiles.cuh load_tiles_q2_0 plus the (already-clean) vecdotq.cuh half. It is CUDA, so it lands unbuilt under the standing 2026-08-18 HQ off-rig ruling and carries NO measurement on this Vulkan-only rig. THE v6 / K-CACHE-MEAN-CENTER VERDICT ORDERED BY LANE-156: **DEFERRED, WITH THE COST NAMED - explicitly NOT declined.** It is backend-agnostic and would therefore work on our Vulkan path (their src/llama-kv-cache.cpp:1304 states the mean is subtracted before K is written and 'nothing else in attention needs to change'), so it is a genuine accuracy lever for quantized KV here. THE COST, MEASURED at prisml/prism against merge-base 8a963fc10: 1076 NEW lines in files we do not have (common/kv-mean-center.cpp 76, common/kv-mean-center.h 30, tools/kv-mean-center/kv-mean-center.cpp 305, tools/kv-mean-center/make-calib-corpus.sh 126, tools/kv-mean-center/README.md 91, tools/kv-mean-center/CMakeLists.txt 8, tests/test-kv-mean-center.cpp 338, docs/kv-mean-center.md 102) PLUS touchpoints in EIGHT shared files (common/arg.cpp, common/common.cpp, common/common.h, include/llama.h, src/llama-context.cpp x6, src/llama-kv-cache.cpp x5, src/llama-kv-cache.h x2, tools/server/server-context.cpp x2) PLUS a PER-MODEL operational cost that no other ingest in this fork has: the feature is inert without a calibration bias GGUF, so every model we want it on needs a calib corpus built and the tool run, and its accuracy claim is unmeasured here until that exists. ORDER OF WORK when it is taken: common/kv-mean-center.{h,cpp} -> the llama-kv-cache load/apply legs -> arg/common wiring -> the tool -> tests -> THEN 4dd165625 -> then one measured q4_0-KV accuracy run on this rig, which is the only number that can justify it. This is a lane, not a rung.",
@@ -185,6 +232,7 @@
       "url": "https://github.com/turbo-tan/llama.cpp-tq3",
       "ref": "tq3/main",
       "pin": "7e24c7caa",
+      "pin_review_2026_08_29_seat46": "PIN HELD at 7e24c7caa, and 47635d703 was NOT ported in this seat. WHY THE PIN IS HELD: 3 allows a re-pin only for SKIP, and 47635d703 ('fix: MTP draft state is per-sequence + roll back draft KV with a single head', #78/#79) is a live, rig-relevant, backend-agnostic TAKE per research/local-inference/2026-08-28-fork-currency-review.md. A blocked-or-unported TAKE forbids a re-pin. WHY IT WAS NOT PORTED HERE: this seat is a 2 base move. 3's own instruction is 'handle one source at a time', and an ingest landed inside a 112-commit base move destroys the attribution of the verify sweep - a newly failing test-backend-ops case could not be attributed to the base or to the port. It also owes its own Taken-from/Origin/Measured-effect trailers, its licenses/ row, and its own full 4. QUEUED, unchanged, as the smallest actionable ingest on the board.",
       "pin_review_2026_08_20_lane161": "ADVANCED 6ff612525 -> 7e24c7caa. Four commits, 2 non-merge, BOTH SKIP with reasons, so the re-pin is lawful under runbook 3. (1) 3bf9074ad 'cuda: force VEC FA kernel for all tq3_0 KV combos (FAULT-008)' - SKIP, SUPERSEDED AT THEIR OWN TIP: b3a8d3697's message says it supersedes the PR #76 workaround and removes both forced-VEC pins, AND our fattn.cu carries zero tq3 pins to begin with (Select-String over ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn.cu for tq3/TQ3/asymm returns nothing). (2) b3a8d3697 'cuda: real tq3_0 strided to_fp16 converter; restore fast FA kernel selection' - SKIP-UNTIL-FEATURE, the prisml-4dd165625 pattern: the FAULT-008 hazard requires tq3_0 AS A KV CACHE TYPE, and our tree has no tq3_0 capability anywhere outside the reserved enum id 49 - no dequantize_block_tq3_0 in convert.cu (only tq3_4s and tq3_1s), no TQ3_0 case in ggml_get_to_fp16_nc_cuda, no tq3_0 in common/ or src/ at all (Grep, zero hits both). The fix patches a capability we have never ingested; it RIDES IN WITH the TQ3_0-KV port (contract ids 48-51 reserve the family), never before it. A 3-way apply was attempted and aborted: their convert.cu predates our lane-160 tq3_idx_from_packed_cuda refactor, so the port must be re-derived in our shape when the feature lands - banked as 09-tq3-b3a8d36-convert-half.patch in the lane-161 evidence dir. STILL OWED, unchanged: afa0f398c and c8b12903e from the older ranges.",
       "pin_review_2026_08_18_lane152": "ADVANCED 58ad80ffb -> 6ff612525. Reviewed 2 commits, 1 non-merge, and it was TAKEN, so the pin moves. b1dd18410 'quantize: keep hybrid-SSM state gates (ssm_alpha/ssm_beta) in f32 by default' - ported verbatim into src/llama-quant.cpp (no ssm_alpha existed anywhere in ours). WHAT WE TOOK IS THE ARCHITECTURAL ARGUMENT, not their benchmark: those tensors participate MULTIPLICATIVELY in the carried recurrent state of a hybrid SSM (DeltaNet / qwen3next), so quantization error compounds along the sequence instead of staying local to one matmul, and the rule that follows - multiplicative state-update participants stay f32, readouts and projections may be quantized - is checkable from the architecture rather than from a number. Their measurement (reasoning depth 17k-64k -> 33k-120k chars, structural codegen bugs eliminated on Qwen3.8-27B at tq3_4s, ~12 MiB per family) is THEIRS on THEIR hardware and is recorded as UNMEASURED on our side; no arm of it was run on this box. STILL OWED FROM THE OLDER RANGE, unchanged by this advance: afa0f398c (server RS-rollback for MTP, their 44.9 -> 61.7 tok/s claim, UNVERIFIED by us) and c8b12903e (TQ3_4S large-K rows_per_block for MTP verify batches). The pin advancing does NOT mean those landed - pin currency and capability ingestion are different axes and this file has conflated them before.",
       "pin_review": "SUPERSEDED IN PART by pin_review_2026_08_17_lane143. Kept verbatim because its TYPE-ID HAZARD half is load-bearing and was re-confirmed live: 'Brings a whole quant family we do not have: TQ3_4S, TQ3_0, TQ3_1S-shift, TQ3_4SE, TQ3_4SV. TYPE-ID HAZARD - it numbers TQ3_1S at 44 and TQ3_4S at 46, and our 46 is TQ4_1S. Its TQ3_4S is 16 B/32 against our TQ4_1S at 20 B/32, so a mix-up fails loudly today; that is luck, not design. YTan2000/Qwen3.8-27B-TQ3_4S-v2.gguf is on disk and cannot load until this is ported.' The branch-coverage half of the old note ('main carries only 7 own commits ... the other ~387 live on feature branches, so a main-only diff UNDERSTATES this fork badly') is REFUTED - see the lane-143 key.",
